    {"id": "history-hearth-way", "first": "PS", "name": "the narrow way behind the History of Magic classroom's cold fireplace", "level": "1", "shape": {"rect": [135.6, 53.4, 136.6, 71.0]}, "about": "1.0 wide in the 2.2 between the classroom's front wall and Transfiguration's passage: from behind the hearth (history-hearth-back) south to a jib door onto the first floor's corridor (history-way-jib), so the way out is always open. a find, not a door that shows: once he has found it, it stays open to him; nothing glows to say tap me (docs/ministry/readers/GL.md); its way out always open. Ledger line 40 (req 481, Interiors' schedule docs/interiors/history-of-magic-classroom.md, The things); Godric's note of 15 October 2026, 5.42 pm (hidden places behind tapestries, cold fireplaces, revolving bookcases, false panels, trapdoors: \"These spaces will bring much delight to the kids\"); ours throughout, books 1 to 3 silent; v29, proposed; settled by Godric's 1 on architect-v29-rooms-1015 (15 October 2026, 6.09 pm: both rooms as drawn, the cold fireplace's way included)", "state": "designed", "cite": ""},
    {"id": "gate-room", "first": "PS", "name": "the room over the gate, the first walls' porters' chamber", "level": "2", "shape": {"rect": [72.0, 59.0, 82.0, 69.0]}, "ceiling": 4.5, "about": "H1: the void over the Entrance Hall's west half (its ceiling 9.7, floor 2's slab to 10.4), between the layout's linen cupboard m (x 68 to 72) and the Astronomy Tower's stair foot g (x 82 to 88), south of the drum; one deep window in the front wall west of the drum (gate-room-window). P2's porters' chamber over the first walls' north gate, cut off when the hall rose two storeys (P4). Ways in: the linen cupboard's back (gate-room-linen) and a wall pretending in g's west wall (gate-room-wall), each the way back out. The same void on 3, 5, 6 and 7 (x 72 to 82, y 59 to 69) is ordinary rooms for the layout's fill on its next run, nothing hidden; on 4 the forgotten classroom and the Muggle Studies room take it. Invented; the hall's ceiling too high to make out (PS 7 L2317). a find, not a door that shows: once he has found it, it stays open to him; nothing glows to say tap me (docs/ministry/readers/GL.md); its way out always open. Ledger line 44 (req 494; Hidden Ways' docs/hidden-ways/batch-1.md, H1); Godric's 1 on hiddenways-batch1-1015 (15 October 2026, 6.11 pm, keep all six); v30", "state": "designed", "cite": ""},
    {"id": "hall-wall-passage", "first": "PS", "name": "the hall's wall passage, at the north windows' sills", "level": "1", "floor": 2.0, "shape": {"rect": [16.4, 70.3, 67.6, 71.1]}, "ceiling": 4.2, "about": "H2: inside the Great Hall's 2.5 m north wall (y 69.5 to 72), 0.8 wide, its floor at +7.2 (the north windows' sills), clear 2.2; floor and ceiling from floor 1's level (5.2 + 2.0 = 7.2, to 9.4). It threads the seven north windows' embrasures (great-hall-window-n1 to -n7, x 23 to 59): in each, the leaded glass on one side and the whole hall on the other over a breast-high stone parapet (hall-wall-parapets); between them a tunnel in the wall. In at the east by a jib door off K's half-landing (k-wall-jib); west through the lug (hall-lug) to its west leg (hall-wall-passage-west). The masons' passage to glaze and clean the high lights (P4), as Hedingham's keep's gallery round its hall; clear of the candles (to 7.0) and the hangings on the piers (the Great Hall lane, 5.58 pm). Canon CoS 5 L8114, PS 7 L2365; the passage invented. a find, not a door that shows: once he has found it, it stays open to him; nothing glows to say tap me (docs/ministry/readers/GL.md); its way out always open. Ledger line 45 (req 494; Hidden Ways' docs/hidden-ways/batch-1.md, H2); Godric's 1 on hiddenways-batch1-1015 (15 October 2026, 6.11 pm, keep all six); v30", "state": "designed", "cite": ""},
    {"id": "hall-lug", "first": "PS", "name": "the lug over the staff table, a listening closet", "level": "1", "floor": 2.0, "shape": {"rect": [15.2, 70.3, 16.4, 71.5]}, "ceiling": 4.2, "about": "H3: at the wall passage's west end, a closet 1.2 by 1.2 in the north wall's thickness at +7.2; to the hall only a small carved stone grille (hall-lug-grille) at about x 16, +7.6, over the staff table's north end, north of and clear of the west wall's banner (Interiors' item 5, y 57.5 to 63.5). A laird's lug as Castle Fraser's (P5). In from the wall passage only; the passage's west leg (hall-wall-passage-west, ours) leaves it on the far side. What drifts up is Events' (req 496): ordinary staff-table talk only, never plot (the orchestrator's condition on the yes). Invented. a find, not a door that shows: once he has found it, it stays open to him; nothing glows to say tap me (docs/ministry/readers/GL.md); its way out always open. Ledger line 46 (req 494; Hidden Ways' docs/hidden-ways/batch-1.md, H3); Godric's 1 on hiddenways-batch1-1015 (15 October 2026, 6.11 pm, keep all six); v30", "state": "designed", "cite": ""},
    {"id": "hall-wall-passage-west", "first": "PS", "name": "the wall passage's west leg, to the West Tower", "level": "1", "floor": 2.0, "shape": {"rect": [7.9, 70.3, 15.2, 71.1]}, "ceiling": 4.2, "about": "H2's way out at the west, routed by the Architect: on from the lug at +7.2 in the same north wall, 2.5 thick here as along the hall (the P2 curtain), so the layout's teacher's study on 1 (x 8 to 15) stops at the wall's inner face (69.5); at x 7.9 it meets the West Tower's drum, and a wall pretending (hall-wall-west-door, PS 8 L2722) opens onto the tower's own stair at its landing nearest +7.2 (the towers list's 'its stair'; the layout's a beside it). a find, not a door that shows: once he has found it, it stays open to him; nothing glows to say tap me (docs/ministry/readers/GL.md); its way out always open. Ledger line 45 (req 494; Hidden Ways' docs/hidden-ways/batch-1.md, H2); Godric's 1 on hiddenways-batch1-1015 (15 October 2026, 6.11 pm, keep all six); v30; the route proposed", "state": "proposed", "cite": "PS 8"},
    {"id": "gate-passage", "first": "PS", "name": "the old gate passage through the Astronomy Tower's foot", "level": "G", "shape": {"rect": [78.0, 70.0, 82.0, 85.0]}, "ceiling": 4.5, "about": "H4's reading of the drum's foot (unresolved in v29): the tower (centre 80, 77; r 8) stands over the front doors, so its foot is pierced by the first walls' north gate, 4 wide, from an open arch at the drum's face (gate-arch, y 85, the top of the front steps) back to the oak front doors (front-doors, y 70), which stay where the books put them; a vaulted porch the boys walk through every day. Its stone keeps the portcullis's groove (portcullis-groove) and three small square murder holes in the vault (murder-holes); the guard room's wall pretending in its west side (guard-room-door). P2's gate, the portcullis last lowered in P4. Canon PS 6 L2286, PS 9 L2949 (the steps and the door); the gate invented. Ledger line 47 (req 494; Hidden Ways' docs/hidden-ways/batch-1.md, H4); Godric's 1 on hiddenways-batch1-1015 (15 October 2026, 6.11 pm, keep all six); v30; the reading proposed", "state": "proposed", "cite": "PS 6, PS 9"},
    {"id": "guard-room", "first": "PS", "name": "the old gate's guard room, in the Astronomy Tower's foot", "level": "G", "shape": {"rect": [74.2, 74.0, 77.6, 80.0]}, "ceiling": 4.5, "about": "H4: west of the gate passage inside the drum's wall (its inner face about r 6.5), 3.4 by 6.0, an arrow loop on the lawn (guard-room-loop); the mural stair up to the portcullis room in the drum's wall to its west (gate-mural-stair), the gun room's stair down at its north end (gun-room-stair). In by the passage's wall pretending (guard-room-door), the way back out; so a loop round by the portcullis room and the tower's spiral. Invented. a find, not a door that shows: once he has found it, it stays open to him; nothing glows to say tap me (docs/ministry/readers/GL.md); its way out always open. Ledger line 47 (req 494; Hidden Ways' docs/hidden-ways/batch-1.md, H4); Godric's 1 on hiddenways-batch1-1015 (15 October 2026, 6.11 pm, keep all six); v30; proposed with the gate's reading", "state": "proposed", "cite": ""},
    {"id": "portcullis-room", "first": "PS", "name": "the portcullis room, across the drum over the gate passage", "level": "1", "shape": {"rect": [74.2, 74.0, 85.8, 80.0]}, "ceiling": 4.5, "about": "H4: on 1 (z 5.2) across the drum over the passage, the old winch (portcullis-winch) and the portcullis's slot in its floor (portcullis-slot), the murder holes' tops beside it. In by the mural stair from the guard room (gate-mural-stair) and by a low door onto the tower's spiral where it passes +5.2 (portcullis-room-spiral, pending ledger 42's turret). Invented. a find, not a door that shows: once he has found it, it stays open to him; nothing glows to say tap me (docs/ministry/readers/GL.md); its way out always open. Ledger line 47 (req 494; Hidden Ways' docs/hidden-ways/batch-1.md, H4); Godric's 1 on hiddenways-batch1-1015 (15 October 2026, 6.11 pm, keep all six); v30; proposed with the gate's reading", "state": "proposed", "cite": ""},
    {"id": "gun-room", "first": "PS", "name": "the gun room under the front steps", "level": "G", "floor": -3.0, "shape": {"rect": [75.0, 85.0, 85.0, 90.0]}, "ceiling": -0.6, "about": "H5: under the top of the front steps (the plans' steps, x 74 to 86, y 85 to 90), a low vault 10 by 5, its floor 3.0 below the doors' sill (the lawn's own level, so the steps climb 15 risers over it) and clear to -0.6; floor and ceiling from the ground floor's level. P4's battery before the gate tower, the steps laid up its face. Its old gun loops are small gratings in the steps' side walls (gun-room-grating-w, -e): daylight, the lawn's air, feet overhead. In by the narrow stair down from the guard room (gun-room-stair), its way back. Canon PS 6 L2286, PS 9 L2949, PoA 16 L19866 (the steps); the room invented. a find, not a door that shows: once he has found it, it stays open to him; nothing glows to say tap me (docs/ministry/readers/GL.md); its way out always open. Ledger line 48 (req 494; Hidden Ways' docs/hidden-ways/batch-1.md, H5); Godric's 1 on hiddenways-batch1-1015 (15 October 2026, 6.11 pm, keep all six); v30; proposed with the gate's reading", "state": "proposed", "cite": ""},
    {"id": "drum-room-6", "first": "PS", "name": "the round room under the common room, the house's old strong room", "level": "6", "shape": {"circle": [42.19, 1.95]}, "r": 5.0, "ceiling": 4.5, "about": "H6: on 6 (z 31.2, clear 4.5) inside Gryffindor Tower's drum (r 6.4, its wall 1.4), 10 across, the floor under the common room (on 7). The layout's sixth-floor storeroom of the house made a find; G to 5 stay storerooms. On 6 the lake-face corridor stops at the drum each side (x 35.8, 48.6) and the way round is north of it, the layout's bend (x 35.8 to 48.6, y 8.35 to 11.35) and its service passage u, confirmed; in by a stretch of the drum's curved wall on that bend that is a wall pretending (drum-room-6-door, PS 8 L2722), the way back out; a window on the lake (drum-room-6-window). P3's strong room under the house's hall, forgotten. Opens nothing into the common room, never bypasses the Fat Lady. Canon PS 7 L2677 (the common room round); invented. a find, not a door that shows: once he has found it, it stays open to him; nothing glows to say tap me (docs/ministry/readers/GL.md); its way out always open. Ledger line 49 (req 494; Hidden Ways' docs/hidden-ways/batch-1.md, H6); Godric's 1 on hiddenways-batch1-1015 (15 October 2026, 6.11 pm, keep all six); v30", "state": "designed", "cite": "PS 8"}
